{"multi_label_scheme__focuses_on__the_likelihood_of_surviving_past_critical_milestones": "The phrase \"focuses on\" indicates that the multi-label scheme directs its predictive efforts towards a particular aspect or outcome. In this context, it emphasizes the scheme's concentration on estimating survival probabilities at discrete time points rather than other potential metrics or outcomes."},
{"the_likelihood_of_surviving_past_critical_milestones": "The likelihood of surviving past critical milestones refers to the probability that a subject will continue to survive beyond specific, significant time points. These milestones are crucial intervals where the event of interest, such as a medical outcome, is evaluated. The multi-label scheme aims to predict these survival probabilities accurately."},
{"multi_label_scheme__has_been_shown_to_yield__higher_accuracy_and_precision_in_prior_research_27": "The phrase \"has been shown to yield\" indicates that the multi-label scheme has demonstrated certain outcomes in previous studies. It suggests a proven effectiveness or result associated with this method."},
{"higher_accuracy_and_precision_in_prior_research_27": "Higher accuracy and precision in prior research [27] refer to the improved performance metrics observed when using the multi-label scheme compared to other methods. This indicates that the scheme provides more reliable and exact predictions in the context of survival analysis."},
{"our_approach": "Our approach refers to the methodology and system developed for matching donors and recipients in the context of organ transplantation. It involves a specific model and framework designed to improve the accuracy and effectiveness of the matching process."},
