{"technical_framework_of_donor_recipient_matching": "The technical framework of donor-recipient matching is a structured system that includes algorithms, models, and processes designed to pair donors with recipients in a way that maximizes compatibility and success rates. In this context, it specifically involves the use of a multi-label XGBoost model adapted for survival analysis, named _Disc-_ _SurvBoost_, which predicts discrete binary survivals and iteratively improves prediction accuracy."},
{"prediction_model": "The prediction model in this context is a technical framework designed for donor-recipient matching, specifically adapted for survival analysis to handle censored individuals. It is named _Disc-_ _SurvBoost_ and is tailored to predict discrete binary survivals.|Here is another description: The prediction model in question is a specialized version of the multi-label XGBoost algorithm, adapted for survival analysis and named _Disc-_ _SurvBoost_. This model is designed to predict discrete binary survival outcomes, leveraging the strengths of tree-based models and gradient boosting to iteratively improve accuracy."},
