{"survival_analysis": "Survival analysis is a branch of statistics focused on analyzing the expected duration of time until one or more events happen, such as death in biological organisms and failure in mechanical systems. In this context, it involves considering censored data, where the event of interest has not occurred for all subjects within the study period."},
{"model__considers__censored_individuals": "The predicate \"considers\" indicates that the model takes into account or includes certain factors in its predictive process. In this context, it specifically refers to the model's capability to handle and make predictions for censored individuals within the survival analysis framework."},
