{"theorem_1": "Theorem 1 is a mathematical statement or proposition that has been proven to be true within the context of the discussion about the DisCScore metric. It specifically addresses a particular property of the DisCScore.|Here is another description: Theorem 1 is a mathematical statement or proposition that has been proven to be true within the context of the study. It serves as a foundational element to support the claims and findings presented in the research."},
{"theorem_1__is_about__lower_bound_property_of_discscore": "The predicate \"is about\" signifies that Theorem 1 pertains to or concerns a specific topic or property, in this case, the Lower-Bound Property of DisCScore. It indicates the subject matter that the theorem aims to establish or prove."},
{"lower_bound_property_of_discscore": "The Lower-Bound Property of DisCScore refers to a characteristic or feature of the DisCScore metric that establishes a minimum threshold or guarantee for the expected survival time in the context of donor-recipient pairs. It is the specific property that Theorem 1 is designed to prove or demonstrate."},
{"discscore__provides__a_lower_bound_on_the_expected_survival_time": "The predicate \"provides\" indicates that DisCScore serves as a tool or method that offers a specific value or estimation. In this context, it means that DisCScore is used to calculate or estimate a particular measure related to the donor-recipient pair."},
{"a_lower_bound_on_the_expected_survival_time": "A lower bound on the expected survival time refers to the minimum estimated duration for which a recipient is expected to survive post-transplantation. This estimation is crucial for assessing the potential success and longevity of the transplant, providing a baseline expectation for patient outcomes."},
{"discscore__satisfies__the_lower_bound_property": "The predicate \"satisfies\" indicates that DisCScore meets or fulfills a certain condition or property, in this case, the Lower-Bound Property, which is a specific characteristic or requirement that DisCScore is designed to adhere to."},
{"the_lower_bound_property": "The Lower-Bound Property is a characteristic or requirement that DisCScore is designed to satisfy. It likely refers to a mathematical or statistical property that ensures DisCScore provides a minimum or baseline value for a certain metric, such as expected survival time, in the context of donor-recipient pairs."},
{"discscore__provides__a_lower_bound_for_the_expected_survival_time": "The predicate \"provides\" indicates that the _DisCScore_ offers a specific value or measure related to the expected survival time, as established by Theorem 1 in the study."},
{"a_lower_bound_for_the_expected_survival_time": "A lower bound for the expected survival time is a minimum value below which the expected survival time will not fall. In the context of the study, the _DisCScore_ ensures that the expected survival time is at least as high as this lower bound."},
{"theorem_1__demonstrates__discscore_provides_a_lower_bound_for_the_expected_survival_time": "The predicate \"demonstrates\" indicates that Theorem 1 provides evidence or proof for a specific claim or relationship. In this context, it shows the validity of the _DisCScore_ as a lower bound for the expected survival time."},
{"discscore_provides_a_lower_bound_for_the_expected_survival_time": "The _DisCScore_ is a compatibility score proposed in the study that is shown to provide a lower bound for the expected survival time. It is statistically significant and positively correlated with survival time, as illustrated in Figure 2 and supported by the proof in Subsection 4.3."},
