{"clinically_meaningful_time_points": "Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These time points are essential for assessing patient outcomes over a diverse range of periods.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as important for assessing patient outcomes after a transplant. These time points are crucial for monitoring and evaluating the success of the transplant over various stages.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals are essential for assessing patient outcomes over a diverse time range.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals are essential for assessing patient outcomes at various stages post-transplant.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals are essential for assessing patient outcomes over a diverse range of time periods."},
