{"expert_clinicians": "Expert clinicians are medical professionals with specialized knowledge and experience in a particular field, such as post-transplant care. They use their expertise to identify and validate clinically meaningful time points for evaluating patient survival.|Here is another description: Expert clinicians are highly skilled medical professionals with specialized knowledge and experience in their respective fields. They play a crucial role in evaluating and making decisions about patient care, as well as contributing to research and development in medical practices.|Here is another description: Expert clinicians are highly skilled medical professionals with extensive knowledge and experience in their respective fields. They play a crucial role in evaluating and interpreting complex medical data.|Here is another description: Expert clinicians are highly trained medical professionals with specialized knowledge and skills in their respective fields. In the context of data cleaning and feature selection for a study, they play a crucial role in evaluating the clinical relevance of variables."},
