{"critical_intervals_for_evaluating_post_transplant_survival": "Critical intervals for evaluating post-transplant survival are specific periods after a transplant that are deemed essential for assessing how well a patient is doing. These intervals help clinicians determine the effectiveness of the transplant and make informed decisions about patient care."},
{"clinically_meaningful_time_points__are__3_6_12_36_60_and_72_months": "The predicate \"are\" signifies the identification and establishment of specific time intervals by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. It indicates that these intervals have been determined and are recognized as important for assessment."},
{"3_6_12_36_60_and_72_months": "The objects 3, 6, 12, 36, 60, and 72 months represent the specific time intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals span a diverse range to capture survival at various stages post-transplant."},
{"clinically_meaningful_time_points__capture__survival_at_a_diverse_time_range": "The predicate \"capture\" in this context signifies the act of measuring or assessing survival outcomes at the identified time points. It implies that these time points are used to gather data on patient survival across a range of intervals."},
{"survival_at_a_diverse_time_range": "Survival at a diverse time range refers to the assessment of patient survival outcomes at multiple, distinct intervals post-transplant. This approach allows for a comprehensive evaluation of survival trends over time, providing a more nuanced understanding of patient prognosis."},
