{"variables_t_1_to_t_6_tm": "Variables _t_ 1 to _t_ 6( _tM_ ) represent the original set of time-based variables used in the study. These variables are substituted with clinically meaningful time points to enhance the relevance and applicability of the survival analysis."},
{"survival_function_s_t": "The survival function _S_ ( _t_ ) represents the probability that a subject will survive beyond a specified time _t_. It is a fundamental concept in survival analysis, used to estimate the likelihood of survival over time."},
