{"organ_procurement_and_transplantation_network_optn_patient_level_information": "The Organ Procurement and Transplantation Network (OPTN) patient-level information refers to detailed data about individual patients involved in liver transplant procedures. This information is collected from all U.S. transplant hospitals and includes both donor and recipient features, sourced from the United Network for Organ Sharing Data (UNOS)."},
{"optn_patient_level_information": "OPTN patient-level information refers to detailed data collected by the Organ Procurement and Transplantation Network on individual patients who have undergone transplant procedures. This information is comprehensive and includes various attributes related to both the donor and the recipient."},
{"optn_patient_level_information__about__lt_procedures_from_all_u_s_transplant_hospitals": "The predicate \"about\" signifies that the subject, OPTN patient-level information, pertains to or is concerned with the object, which in this case are LT procedures from all U.S. transplant hospitals. It indicates a relationship where the subject provides specific details or data regarding the object."},
{"lt_procedures_from_all_u_s_transplant_hospitals": "LT procedures from all U.S. transplant hospitals refer to liver transplant operations performed across various transplant centers in the United States. These procedures are documented with detailed patient-level information, including features of both the donors and recipients, as part of the STAR files dataset."},
{"lt_procedures": "LT procedures refer to liver transplant processes documented in the STAR files, which are comprehensive datasets containing patient-level information from U.S. transplant hospitals."},
{"lt_procedures__include__both_donor_and_recipient_features": "The predicate \"include\" signifies that the LT procedures documented in the STAR files encompass a range of detailed information. This information is essential for analyzing and understanding the outcomes and processes involved in liver transplants."},
{"both_donor_and_recipient_features": "Both donor and recipient features refer to the comprehensive set of data points collected for both the individuals donating the livers and those receiving them. This includes various medical, demographic, and procedural details that are critical for the analysis of transplant outcomes."},
{"features": "The features refer to the specific data points or attributes collected from liver transplant procedures, including both donor and recipient information. These features are crucial for analyzing and understanding the outcomes and trends in liver transplantation.|Here is another description: The features in question are elements within a dataset that underwent a cleaning and refinement process. These features were subject to various statistical assessments to determine their suitability for further analysis.|Here is another description: The features refer to the top 20 most frequently selected attributes in the _DiscSurvBoost_ model, which are detailed in Fig 3 and Appendix B. These features are crucial for the model's predictions and are integral to its interpretability and effectiveness."},
