{"united_network_for_organ_sharing_data_unos": "The United Network for Organ Sharing Data (UNOS) is a comprehensive database that contains patient-level information about organ transplantation procedures in the United States. It serves as a critical source for research and analysis in the field of organ transplantation."},
{"data_recording": "Data recording refers to the process of collecting and storing information from STAR files, which contain patient-level data about liver transplant procedures from U.S. transplant hospitals. This data includes both donor and recipient features and is sourced from the United Network for Organ Sharing Data (UNOS)."},
