{"hyperparameter_\u03b1": "The hyperparameter _\u03b1_ is a specific parameter within a machine learning model that influences its performance. In this context, it is a critical factor that needs to be optimized to achieve the best model performance."},
{"hyperparameter_\u03b1__considered__ten_uniformly_spaced_values_in_the_interval_0_1": "The predicate \"considered\" indicates the action of evaluating or taking into account different values for the hyperparameter _\u03b1_. This process is essential for determining which value of _\u03b1_ leads to the optimal performance of the model."},
{"ten_uniformly_spaced_values_in_the_interval_0_1": "The object \"ten uniformly spaced values in the interval (0 _,_ 1)\" refers to a set of ten distinct values that are evenly distributed between 0 and 1. These values are candidates for the hyperparameter _\u03b1_, and the model's performance is assessed for each of these values to find the best one."},
