{"fig_3": "Fig 3 is a figure within the document that visually represents the top 20 most frequently selected features by the _DiscSurvBoost_ model. This figure is essential for providing a clear and concise overview of the features that the model deems most important, aiding in the interpretability and credibility of the model's outputs."},
{"features__align_closely_with__clinical_variables": "The phrase \"align closely with\" indicates a strong correspondence or similarity between the features selected by the _DiscSurvBoost_ model and the clinical variables that medical practitioners typically consider in their decision-making processes for transplants."},
{"clinical_variables": "Clinical variables are the specific medical factors and metrics that healthcare professionals use to assess patient conditions and make informed decisions. In the context of transplants, these variables might include patient health status, donor compatibility, and other relevant medical data."},
{"model_s_outputs": "The model\u2019s outputs refer to the results generated by the _DiscSurvBoost_ model, which are based on the top 20 most frequently selected features that align with clinical variables used in transplant decision-making."},
