{"empirically_robust_and_clinically_credible": "Empirically robust and clinically credible describes the qualities of the model\u2019s outputs. Empirically robust means that the outputs are consistently reliable based on observed data, while clinically credible indicates that they are trusted and accepted by medical practitioners for use in real-world scenarios."},
{"harrell_s_c_statistic": "Harrell\u2019s C-statistic is a measure used to evaluate the discriminatory power of a model, particularly in survival analysis. It indicates how well a model can distinguish between individuals with different survival times."},
{"harrell_s_c_statistic__is_calculated_for__the_entire_study_period_2009_to_2019": "The phrase \"is calculated for\" indicates the process of determining the value of Harrell\u2019s C-statistic specifically for a defined period, in this case, the entire study period from 2009 to 2019."},
