{"time_dependent_receiver_operating_characteristic_curve_roc": "The time-dependent Receiver Operating Characteristic Curve (ROC) is a graphical representation used to evaluate the performance of a survival model at different time points. It plots the true positive rate against the false positive rate to show how well the model can distinguish between events and non-events over time."},
