{"regression_models_and_life_tables": "'Regression models and life-tables' is a seminal paper published by D. R. Cox in 1972, which introduced the Cox proportional hazards model, a widely used statistical technique for analyzing survival data.|Here is another description: \"Regression models and life-tables\" is a seminal paper authored by D. R. Cox, which introduces proportional hazards models for survival analysis. This work has had a profound impact on statistical methods used in medical research and other fields where time-to-event data is analyzed.|Here is another description: \"Regression models and life-tables\" is a seminal paper authored by D. R. Cox, which introduced proportional hazards models for survival analysis. This work has had a profound impact on statistical methods used in medical research and other fields where time-to-event data is analyzed.|Here is another description: \"Regression models and life-tables\" is a seminal paper authored by D. R. Cox, published in the Journal of the Royal Statistical Society: Series B (Methodological) in 1972. The paper introduces and discusses the application of regression models to life-tables, which are statistical tables that show the probability of death of an individual at a specific age."},
