{"random_survival_forests": "\"Random survival forests\" is a methodological paper published in 2008 that introduces a new ensemble learning technique for survival analysis, which is an extension of the random forest algorithm to handle censored data commonly found in survival studies.|Here is another description: \"Random survival forests\" is a methodological paper published in 2008 that introduces a new statistical technique for survival analysis, which is an extension of the random forest algorithm to handle right-censored survival data.|Here is another description: \"Random survival forests\" is a methodological paper published in 2008 that introduces a new statistical approach for survival analysis, which is an extension of the random forest algorithm to handle right-censored survival data.|Here is another description: \"Random survival forests\" is a statistical method developed for survival analysis, which was co-authored by M. S. Lauer along with H. Ishwaran, U. B. Kogalur, and E. H. Blackstone.|Here is another description: Random survival forests are a statistical method used for survival analysis, which is a branch of statistics that deals with time-to-event data. This method extends the concept of random forests to handle censored data, which is common in survival studies."},
