{"living_donor_cases": "Living-donor cases refer to liver transplant procedures where the liver is donated by a living individual, as opposed to a deceased donor. These cases are a subset of liver transplant procedures and are considered in the context of cohort selection for research or analysis."},
{"living_donor_cases__exclusion_from__unos_liver_transplants": "Exclusion from indicates the process of removing or not including certain cases from a larger dataset or study. In this context, it refers to the removal of living-donor cases from the total number of UNOS liver transplants to refine the dataset for further analysis."},
{"multiorgan_cases": "Multiorgan cases refer to medical procedures where more than one organ is transplanted simultaneously. In the context of liver transplants, these cases involve the transplantation of the liver along with other organs, which can complicate the procedure and affect outcomes."},
{"multiorgan_cases__exclusion_from__unos_liver_transplants": "Exclusion from signifies the process of removing certain cases from a dataset or study. In this context, it means that multiorgan cases were not included in the UNOS liver transplants dataset used for analysis, likely due to their complexity and potential impact on study results."},
{"temporarily_inactive_cases": "Temporarily inactive cases refer to instances within the UNOS liver transplant data where the transplant process was halted or paused for a period, possibly due to various medical or logistical reasons."},
{"temporarily_inactive_cases__exclusion_from__unos_liver_transplants": "Exclusion from signifies the process of removing or not considering certain cases from a dataset or study. In this context, it means that temporarily inactive cases were not included in the final count or analysis of UNOS liver transplants."},
{"missing_survival_cases": "Missing-survival cases refer to instances within the UNOS liver transplant dataset where survival data is not available or recorded. These cases are part of the broader dataset but lack critical information necessary for certain analyses."},
{"missing_survival_cases__exclusion_from__unos_liver_transplants": "Exclusion from signifies the process of removing specific cases or data points from a larger dataset. In this context, it involves omitting cases with missing survival data from the UNOS liver transplants to ensure the integrity and reliability of the analysis."},
