{"article": "The article in question is a scholarly work that discusses the development and validation of a method to improve posttransplant survival rates and reduce adverse outcomes in liver transplants. It introduces a compatibility score called _DisCScore_ and uses a multi-label variant of XGBoost with a survival loss function named _DiscSurvBoost_.|Here is another description: The subject, \"article,\" refers to a scholarly or professional piece of writing, typically published in a journal or similar platform, that presents research findings, analysis, or discussions on a specific topic. In this context, the article is authored by individuals listed above and pertains to research on liver transplant data and the development of a compatibility score for donor-patient pairings.|Here is another description: The article in question is a scholarly work that discusses the development and validation of a method for improving posttransplant survival rates and reducing adverse outcomes in liver transplants. It introduces a compatibility score called _DisCScore_, which is derived using a specialized machine learning model."},
{"article__is_copyrighted_by__author_s": "The predicate \"is copyrighted by\" signifies the legal ownership and rights over the intellectual property of the article. It indicates that the author(s) hold the copyright, which includes the right to reproduce, distribute, display, and make derivative works based on the article."},
