{"a_probability_that_captures_how_likely_the_event_will_occur_within_each_interval": "A probability that captures how likely the event will occur within each interval represents the output of the model's learning process. This probability is a quantitative measure that reflects the likelihood of a specific event, such as patient survival, happening within predefined time frames. It is crucial for making informed decisions and assessments in clinical settings."},
{"multi_label_scheme": "The multi-label scheme refers to a method where each discrete time point is treated as a separate label in the prediction model. This approach allows the model to estimate the probability of an event occurring within each interval, rather than trying to predict the exact time of the event.|Here is another description: The multi-label scheme is a method used in predictive modeling where each discrete time point is treated as a separate label. This approach allows the model to estimate the probability of an event occurring within each interval.|Here is another description: The multi-label scheme refers to a method where each time point in a series is modeled as a separate label, allowing the model to estimate the probability of surviving past critical milestones."},
{"multi_label_scheme__is__generally_more_straightforward_to_estimate": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies that the multi-label scheme has a certain characteristic or property. Specifically, it indicates that this scheme possesses the quality of being generally more straightforward to estimate compared to other methods."},
{"generally_more_straightforward_to_estimate": "Generally more straightforward to estimate means that the multi-label scheme is easier to implement and compute compared to other methods, such as direct estimation of a single risk score. This ease of estimation is attributed to its focus on the likelihood of surviving past critical milestones, which has been shown to yield higher accuracy and precision."},
{"multi_label_scheme__focuses_on__the_likelihood_of_surviving_past_critical_milestones": "The phrase \"focuses on\" indicates that the multi-label scheme directs its predictive efforts towards a specific aspect or outcome. In this context, it emphasizes the scheme's concentration on estimating survival probabilities at various time points."},
{"the_likelihood_of_surviving_past_critical_milestones": "The likelihood of surviving past critical milestones refers to the probability that a subject will survive beyond certain significant time points. These milestones are discrete intervals where the model predicts the chances of survival, contributing to higher accuracy and precision in the predictions."},
