{"higher_accuracy_and_precision_in_prior_research_27": "Higher accuracy and precision in prior research [27] refer to the improved performance metrics observed when the multi-label scheme was employed. This means that the scheme resulted in more reliable and exact predictions in previous studies."},
{"our_approach": "Our approach refers to the methodology and system developed for matching donors with recipients in the context of organ transplantation. It involves the use of advanced machine learning techniques to improve the accuracy and efficiency of the matching process."},
{"our_approach__details__technical_framework_of_donor_recipient_matching": "The term \"details\" in this context signifies a comprehensive explanation or breakdown of the components and processes involved in the technical framework. It implies a thorough exposition of how the approach is structured and functions."},
{"technical_framework_of_donor_recipient_matching": "The technical framework of donor-recipient matching is a sophisticated system that utilizes multi-label XGBoost, a machine learning model adapted for survival analysis, to predict the compatibility and survival outcomes of potential donor-recipient pairs. This framework is designed to enhance the precision of matching by considering various factors and censored data."},
{"prediction_model": "The prediction model in question is a specialized tool designed for donor-recipient matching in the context of survival analysis, specifically tailored to handle censored data. It is named _Disc-_ _SurvBoost_, highlighting its capability to predict discrete binary survival outcomes.|Here is another description: The prediction model in question is a specialized version of XGBoost, adapted for survival analysis and named _Disc-_ _SurvBoost_. It is designed to predict discrete binary survival outcomes and leverages the strengths of tree-based models combined with gradient boosting for iterative improvement."},
{"prediction_model__is__multi_label_xgboost": "The predicate \"is\" signifies the identification or classification of the prediction model as a specific type, in this case, a multi-label XGBoost model. This relation underscores the model's nature and the methodology it employs."},
{"multi_label_xgboost": "Multi-label XGBoost is a machine learning model that extends the XGBoost algorithm to handle multi-label classification tasks. It combines the strengths of tree-based models with gradient boosting, iteratively improving prediction accuracy by building each tree to correct the errors of the previous ones.|Here is another description: Multi-label XGBoost is a machine learning model that extends the traditional XGBoost algorithm to handle multiple labels or outcomes. It is particularly useful in scenarios where a single input can be associated with more than one output category."},
{"multi_label_xgboost__is_adapted_to__survival_analysis": "The phrase \"is adapted to\" indicates a modification or customization of the multi-label XGBoost model to suit a specific application or context, in this case, survival analysis. This adaptation involves altering the model to effectively handle the unique challenges and data characteristics associated with survival analysis."},
{"survival_analysis": "Survival analysis is a branch of statistics focused on analyzing the expected duration of time until one or more events happen, such as death in biological organisms and failure in mechanical systems. In the context of the triple, it refers to the specific application domain to which the multi-label XGBoost model has been adapted, particularly to account for censored data where the event of interest has not occurred for some individuals by the end of the study period.|Here is another description: Survival analysis is a branch of statistics focused on analyzing the expected duration of time until one or more events happen, such as death in biological organisms and failure in mechanical systems. It uses various metrics, including the C-index, to evaluate model performance."},
