{"disc_survboost": "Disc-SurvBoost is the name given to the model to highlight its capability to predict discrete binary survival outcomes, emphasizing its discrete nature and its application in survival analysis.|Here is another description: Disc-SurvBoost is a specialized model adapted from multi-label XGBoost for survival analysis, specifically designed to handle censored individuals in donor-recipient matching. It emphasizes the prediction of outcomes at discrete time points."},
{"disc_survboost__predicts__discrete_binary_survivals": "The predicate \"predicts\" in this context refers to the capability of the Disc-SurvBoost model to forecast outcomes. It indicates that the model is used to make predictions about future events, specifically discrete binary survivals in the context of donor-recipient matching."},
{"discrete_binary_survivals": "Discrete binary survivals refer to the outcomes predicted by the Disc-SurvBoost model, which are binary in nature (e.g., survival or non-survival) and assessed at specific, discrete time points. These predictions are crucial for evaluating the compatibility of donors and recipients in transplant scenarios."},
{"tree_based_model": "The tree-based model refers to a type of machine learning model that uses tree structures to make predictions. In the context provided, it is specifically adapted for survival analysis and is part of the _Disc-_ _SurvBoost_ model, which predicts discrete binary survivals."},
