{"clinically_meaningful_time_points": "Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified as critical for assessing post-transplant survival. These time points are essential for evaluating patient outcomes over a diverse range of time frames.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as important for assessing patient outcomes after a medical procedure, such as a transplant. These time points are selected to capture a comprehensive view of patient survival across a varied timeline.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals are essential for assessing patient outcomes over a diverse range of time periods.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals are essential for assessing patient outcomes at various stages after the transplant.|Here is another description: Clinically meaningful time points refer to specific intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals are essential for assessing patient outcomes over a diverse time range."},
