{"critical_intervals_for_evaluating_post_transplant_survival": "Critical intervals for evaluating post-transplant survival are specific periods after a transplant that are crucial for assessing how well a patient is doing. These intervals, such as 3, 6, 12, 36, 60, and 72 months, help clinicians monitor and analyze patient recovery and long-term outcomes."},
{"clinically_meaningful_time_points__are__3_6_12_36_60_and_72_months": "The predicate \"are\" signifies the identification and establishment of specific time intervals by expert clinicians as significant for evaluating post-transplant survival. It indicates that these intervals have been determined and recognized as important for clinical assessment."},
{"3_6_12_36_60_and_72_months": "The objects 3, 6, 12, 36, 60, and 72 months represent the specific time intervals identified by expert clinicians as critical for evaluating post-transplant survival. These intervals span a diverse range, allowing for comprehensive assessment of patient outcomes at various stages post-transplant."},
