{"data_from_star_files": "Data from STAR files refers to information collected from the Standard Transplant Analysis and Research files, which contain detailed patient-level data about liver transplant procedures, including donor and recipient characteristics, sourced from the Organ Procurement and Transplantation Network."},
{"star_files": "STAR files are a standardized dataset used in the study of liver transplants, providing comprehensive information from U.S. transplant hospitals. They are a critical resource for researchers analyzing transplant outcomes and patient data.|Here is another description: STAR files are datasets that contain Organ Procurement and Transplantation Network (OPTN) patient-level information about liver transplant (LT) procedures from all U.S. transplant hospitals. They are part of the Standard Transplant Analysis and Research (STAR) program and are sourced from the United Network for Organ Sharing Data (UNOS)."},
{"star_files__are__datasets_containing_optn_patient_level_information_about_lt_procedures": "The predicate \"are\" in this context signifies the nature or identity of the STAR files, indicating that they serve as a specific type of dataset. It establishes the relationship between the subject (STAR files) and the object (datasets containing OPTN patient-level information about LT procedures)."},
{"datasets_containing_optn_patient_level_information_about_lt_procedures": "Datasets containing OPTN patient-level information about LT procedures are comprehensive collections of data that include detailed records about liver transplant patients. These datasets are crucial for analyzing transplant-related outcomes and patient features, sourced from the United Network for Organ Sharing Data (UNOS)."},
{"star_files__include__donor_and_recipient_features": "The predicate 'include' signifies that the STAR files contain or comprise certain elements. In this context, it indicates that the STAR files are comprehensive datasets that encompass various features related to liver transplants."},
{"donor_and_recipient_features": "Donor and recipient features refer to the specific characteristics and data points related to both the donors and recipients involved in liver transplant procedures. These features are crucial for analyzing transplant outcomes and understanding the factors that influence them."},
{"data": "The data refers to the datasets used in the study, specifically from STAR (Standard Transplant Analysis and Research) files, which contain detailed patient-level information about liver transplant procedures."},
{"data__collated_from__unos": "The predicate \"collated from\" indicates the process by which the data was gathered and organized. It suggests that the data was collected and compiled from a specific source to be used in the study."},
{"unos": "UNOS, or the United Network for Organ Sharing, is the organization from which the data was collated. UNOS manages the nation's organ transplant system under a federal contract and is responsible for maintaining the Organ Procurement and Transplantation Network (OPTN) database.|Here is another description: The United Network for Organ Sharing (UNOS) is an organization that manages the organ transplant system in the United States, facilitating the donation and transplantation of organs."},
