{"we__performed__the_train_test_split_using_10_different_random_seeds": "The predicate \"performed\" indicates the action taken by the subject. In this context, it means that the researchers carried out the process of dividing the dataset into training and testing sets multiple times using different random seeds."},
{"the_train_test_split_using_10_different_random_seeds": "The object \"the train-test split using 10 different random seeds\" describes the specific action performed by the subject. It involves creating multiple train-test splits of the dataset, each with a different random seed, to ensure variability and robustness in the experimental results."},
{"we__aggregated__the_performance_results": "\"Aggregated\" in this context means that the researchers combined or summarized the performance results obtained from multiple runs of the experiments. This was done to provide a comprehensive and reliable assessment of the discriminative capability of the models being compared."},
{"the_performance_results": "\"The performance results\" refers to the outcomes or metrics (such as accuracy, precision, recall, or other relevant measures) obtained from the experiments. These results were aggregated to ensure robustness and reliability in the comparison of different models."},
{"we__run_our_experiments__with_different_random_seeds": "\"Run our experiments\" indicates the action taken by the subject, which involves executing the experiments. This predicate shows the process of conducting the experiments as part of the research methodology."},
{"with_different_random_seeds": "\"With different random seeds\" describes the manner in which the experiments are conducted. Using different random seeds ensures variability and randomness in the experimental setup, which is crucial for obtaining reliable and robust results."},
{"we__obtained__a_sufficient_number_of_runs_for_reliable_95_confidence_intervals": "The predicate \"obtained\" indicates that the subject successfully acquired or achieved something through their actions. In this context, it means that the researchers were able to gather or secure a specific outcome from their experimental process."},
{"a_sufficient_number_of_runs_for_reliable_95_confidence_intervals": "The object \"a sufficient number of runs for reliable 95% confidence intervals\" describes the outcome that the researchers obtained. It refers to the adequate quantity of experimental runs that were necessary to ensure the reliability of the 95% confidence intervals in their results, which is a statistical measure indicating the precision and reliability of the estimates."},
{"we__demonstrated__robustness": "\"Demonstrated\" indicates that the authors or researchers have shown or proven something through their experiments and analysis. In this case, they have shown the robustness of their approach by running experiments with different random seeds and obtaining reliable 95% confidence intervals."},
{"robustness": "\"Robustness\" in this context refers to the reliability and consistency of the performance results obtained by the authors or researchers. It indicates that the results are not heavily dependent on a specific random seed or experimental setup, and that the approach is able to produce consistent and reliable results across different runs."},
{"we__assessed__the_discriminative_capability_between_optimal_and_suboptimal_dr_pairs_of_discscore_against_other_benchmarks": "\"Assessed\" indicates that the researchers evaluated or measured the performance or effectiveness of something. In this context, it means they conducted an evaluation to determine how well _DisCScore_ discriminates between optimal and suboptimal DR pairs compared to other benchmarks."},
{"the_discriminative_capability_between_optimal_and_suboptimal_dr_pairs_of_discscore_against_other_benchmarks": "The discriminative capability between optimal and suboptimal DR pairs of _DisCScore_ against other benchmarks refers to the ability of _DisCScore_ to distinguish between optimal and suboptimal DR pairs more effectively than other benchmarks. These benchmarks include clinical scores like DMELD and BAR, statistical models like CoxPH and RSF, and neural network-based approaches like DeepSurv and DeepHit."},
{"we__included__clinical_scores_like_dmeld_3_and_balance_of_risk_bar_4": "\"Included\" signifies that the authors or researchers have incorporated or taken into account certain elements or benchmarks in their study or experiment. In this case, they have included clinical scores like DMELD and Balance of Risk (BAR) among other benchmarks for comparison."},
{"clinical_scores_like_dmeld_3_and_balance_of_risk_bar_4": "\"Clinical scores like DMELD [3], and Balance of Risk (BAR) [4]\" are benchmarks used in the study or experiment to assess the discriminative capability of _DisCScore_. DMELD and BAR are clinical scoring systems that likely evaluate the risk or prognosis of certain medical conditions, serving as standards for comparison against other models like CoxPH, RSF, DeepSurv, and DeepHit."},
{"we__included__the_classical_statistical_cox_proportional_hazards_coxph_model_15": "The predicate \"included\" indicates that the subject has incorporated or added a specific model or method into their study or comparison. This action suggests that the model is one of several approaches being evaluated."},
{"the_classical_statistical_cox_proportional_hazards_coxph_model_15": "The object \"the classical statistical Cox proportional hazards (CoxPH) model [15]\" is a well-established statistical method used for survival analysis. It is included in the study to compare its performance against other benchmarks, such as clinical scores and machine learning models, in assessing the discriminative capability between optimal and suboptimal DR pairs."},
{"we__included__tree_based_model_random_survival_forest_rsf_20": "The predicate \"included\" indicates that the subject (the researchers) incorporated or added a specific model into their experiments or comparisons. This action suggests that the model was considered relevant and necessary for the comprehensive evaluation of the study's objectives."},
{"tree_based_model_random_survival_forest_rsf_20": "The object \"tree-based model Random Survival Forest (RSF) [20]\" is a specific type of statistical model used in survival analysis. It is a tree-based ensemble method that combines multiple decision trees to predict the time-to-event outcomes. The inclusion of this model in the study demonstrates the researchers' intention to compare it with other benchmarks to assess its performance and discriminative capability."},
{"we__included__more_recent_neural_network_based_approaches_deepsurv_and_deephit_8_16": "The predicate \"included\" indicates that the authors have incorporated or added certain elements into their comparison benchmarks. This action signifies that the authors are ensuring a comprehensive evaluation by including a wide range of approaches."},
{"more_recent_neural_network_based_approaches_deepsurv_and_deephit_8_16": "The object \"more recent neural network based approaches DeepSurv and DeepHit [8, 16]\" refers to advanced machine learning methods that utilize neural networks for survival analysis. These approaches are part of the benchmarks against which _DisCScore_ is being compared to demonstrate its effectiveness and robustness."},
{"we__provided__a_comprehensive_comparison": "The predicate \"provided\" indicates the action taken by the subject to offer or supply something. In this context, it signifies that the authors have supplied or presented a certain type of comparison as part of their study."},
{"a_comprehensive_comparison": "The object \"a comprehensive comparison\" refers to the detailed and thorough evaluation or analysis that the authors have conducted. This comparison involves assessing the discriminative capability of _DisCScore_ against various benchmarks, including clinical scores, statistical models, and neural network-based approaches."},
{"xgboost__has_property__transparency_and_interpretability": "The predicate \"has_property\" indicates that XGBoost possesses certain characteristics or attributes that are significant for its application. In this context, it highlights the inherent qualities that make XGBoost suitable for specific uses."},
{"transparency_and_interpretability": "Transparency and interpretability are critical properties for machine learning models, especially in fields like medicine. They allow practitioners to understand how the model arrives at its predictions, which is essential for trust and adoption in clinical settings."},
{"top_20_most_frequently_selected_features": "The top 20 most frequently selected features refer to the most commonly chosen attributes or variables by the _DiscSurvBoost_ model in its analysis. These features are critical as they closely align with the clinical variables considered by practitioners in making transplant decisions, thereby enhancing the model's clinical credibility."},
{"top_20_most_frequently_selected_features__are_presented_in__fig_3": "The phrase \"are presented in\" indicates that the top 20 most frequently selected features are visually or systematically shown in a specific location within the document. This presentation helps readers easily access and understand the features that the model deems most significant."},
