{"our_score__differentiates__recipients_who_surpass_early_critical_thresholds_for_filtering_out_suboptimal_donors": "Differentiates in this context means to distinguish or identify the differences between recipients who are likely to have better outcomes and those who are not. The score is used to make this distinction more effectively."},
{"recipients_who_surpass_early_critical_thresholds_for_filtering_out_suboptimal_donors": "Recipients who surpass early critical thresholds for filtering out suboptimal donors are those individuals who, based on the score, are predicted to have better outcomes and are therefore selected over others who do not meet these thresholds. This helps in ensuring that only the most suitable donors are chosen."},
